
### 1. Request Access Token
POST {{keycloakserver}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username={{user1_username}}&password={{user1_password}}&client_id={{jwtClient}}&client_secret={{jwtClientSecret}}&grant_type=password&scope=openid

> {%
    if (response.status === 200) {
        client.global.set("user1_access_token", response.body.access_token);
        client.global.set("user1_refresh_token", response.body.refresh_token);
    }
%}


### 2. Get Authenticated User Information
GET {{keycloakserver}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/userinfo
Authorization: Bearer {{user1_access_token}}


### 3. Check Access Token Status
# Expected: "active": true for a valid token with the required audience.
POST {{keycloakserver}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token/introspect
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{jwtClient}}&client_secret={{jwtClientSecret}}&token={{user1_access_token}}&token_type_hint=access_token


### 4. Call Secured REST API
# Change the URL to the REST API you want to test.
GET http://localhost:8090/restapi/students
Authorization: Bearer {{user1_access_token}}


### 5. Logout
# Ends the Keycloak session associated with the refresh token.
POST {{keycloakserver}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/logout
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{jwtClient}}&client_secret={{jwtClientSecret}}&refresh_token={{user1_refresh_token}}


### 6. Test Access Token After Logout
# Reuse the original access token after logging out.
#
# The API may still return HTTP 200 OK until the JWT expires.
# MicroProfile JWT validates the token locally without
# contacting Keycloak to check whether the user logged out.

GET http://localhost:8090/restapi/students
Authorization: Bearer {{user1_access_token}}
